      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "In rectangular coordinates, $(x, y, z) = (0, -3 \\sqrt{3}, 3)$\n\nTo find the corresponding spherical coordinates $(\\rho, \\theta, \\phi)$, we can use the following formulas:\n\n1. $\\rho = \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2}$\n2. $\\theta = \\arctan\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)$ (with consideration of the quadrant)\n3. $\\phi = \\arccos\\left(\\frac{z}{\\rho}\\right)$\n\nUsing these formulas:\n\n1. $\\rho = \\sqrt{(0)^2 + (-3 \\sqrt{3})^2 + 3^2} = \\sqrt{0 + 27 + 9} = \\sqrt{36} = 6$\n\n2. $\\theta = \\arctan\\left(\\frac{-3 \\sqrt{3}}{0}\\right) = \\arctan\\left(\\frac{-3 \\sqrt{3}}{0}\\right)$ However, since $x=0$ and $y < 0$, $\\theta = \\pi$.\n\n3. $\\phi = \\arccos\\left(\\frac{3}{6}\\right) = \\arccos\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$\n\nTherefore, the spherical coordinates are $(\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\boxed{(6, \\pi, \\frac{\\pi}{3})}$.",
